  "id": "taste-pore",
  "term": "taste pore",
  "definition": "A taste pore is the opening at the top of a taste bud where the taste cell microvilli face the saliva and detect chemicals in food. It is the apical region where taste receptors are located, kept separate from the parts of the cells that send signals to nerve fibers.",
